      "id": "vuq3q6c",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Factors Affecting Natural Vegetation"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Natural vegetation in India is shaped by various climatic and geographical factors.",
        "The major vegetation types include Tropical Evergreen, Tropical Deciduous, Thorn, Mountain, and Mangrove Forests.",
        "Tropical Deciduous forests represent the most widespread forest type in India.",
        "Mangrove forests thrive in coastal tidal regions with specialized salt-tolerant root systems.",
        "Natural vegetation plays a vital role in maintaining ecological balance and supporting wildlife."
      ],
      "id": "l8n7smk"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5hfd9oj",
      "content": "• Climate – Temperature and rainfall determine vegetation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7vzfwld",
      "content": "• Soil – Different soils support different plants."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sdjaz5q",
      "content": "• Relief – Plains, plateaus and mountains influence vegetation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xdppsvx",
      "content": "• Altitude – Vegetation changes with height in mountain regions."
    },
    {
